        "sql.case_expressions"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Let's revisit",
      "title": "The simple CASE form: CASE expression WHEN value THEN result … END",
      "lede": "The expression is written once after CASE; each WHEN lists only the comparison value.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "In the simple CASE form, the expression to test is placed once, right after the CASE keyword. Each WHEN then lists only the value to compare against — the equality check is implicit. `CASE region WHEN 'north' THEN 'N' WHEN 'south' THEN 'S' ELSE 'O' END` is equivalent to writing `CASE WHEN region = 'north' THEN 'N' WHEN region = 'south' THEN 'S' ELSE 'O' END`. Use the simple form when every branch tests the same expression against a different value.",
          "role": "mechanism",
